      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To generate tests for the scenario \"\u7528\u6237\u8d2d\u4e70\u5546\u54c1\" (User purchases a product), I'll extract the requirements and create pytest-compatible test cases. Let's outline the typical steps for this scenario:\n\n1. User selects a product.\n2. User adds the product to the cart.\n3. User proceeds to checkout.\n4. User enters payment details.\n5. User confirms the purchase.\n6. System processes the payment.\n7. System confirms the order.\n\nBased on these steps, I'll create pytest test cases. Here's the code:\n\n```python\nimport pytest\n\ndef test_user_selects_product():\n    # Simulate user selecting a product\n    product = \"Product A\"\n    assert product is not None\n\ndef test_user_adds_product_to_cart(cart):\n    # Simulate adding product to cart\n    product = \"Product A\"\n    cart.add(product)\n    assert product in cart\n\ndef test_user_proceeds_to_checkout(cart):\n    # Simulate proceeding to checkout\n    assert cart.is_ready_for_checkout()\n\ndef test_user_enters_payment_details(payment_system):\n    # Simulate entering payment details\n    payment_details = {\n        \"card_number\": \"1234 5678 9012 3456\",\n        \"expiry_date\": \"12/26\",\n        \"cvv\": \"123\"\n    }\n    assert payment_system.validate(payment_details)\n\ndef test_user_confirms_purchase(order_system):\n    # Simulate confirming the purchase\n    result = order_system.confirm_purchase()\n    assert result == \"Purchase Confirmed\"\n\ndef test_system_processes_payment(payment_system):\n    # Simulate payment processing\n    result = payment_system.process()\n    assert result == \"Payment Successful\"\n\ndef test_system_confirms_order(order_system):\n    # Simulate order confirmation\n    result = order_system.confirm_order()\n    assert result == \"Order Confirmed\"\n```\n\nThese tests assume the existence of `cart`, `payment_system`, and `order_system` objects, which should be properly initialized in your test setup. Let me know if you need any modifications or further assistance!",
